Z||000000||SlingBlade||07-30-2001||08:16 PM||||I have an ECM question for which I was unable to determine the answer looking in the PFF archives.  I have a complete V6/4spd combo from an 86 GT, but I need an ECM and wiring harness to put in my 87 coupe.  I know that 86-88 has the 7170 and the 85 has the 6869. Do I need a 7170 that has the manual chipset specific to the 4spd (if there is such a thing) or will any manual-chip 7170 make do? Or does 4spd require the 6869?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||JayUSA77||07-30-2001||08:45 PM||||are you talking about putting a chip in the ECM to make it work for your setup or getting the complete ECM. Well in any case get a ECM for the V-6 and 4spd.  YOu find alot on ebay for around 15 bucks if you lucky<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||07-30-2001||09:22 PM||||Use ECM and chip for the V-6 4 speed cars.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||07-30-2001||09:25 PM||||Technically, you need a 4 spd chip to go with a 4spd trans, but if you use a 5spd or vice-versa, the shift light will be off but nothing else will be affected. Don't sweat that.<P>The chip determines auto or manual trans. The ECM just does what the chip tells it to. There are 6869 in 85 used with auto and manual. Same for the 7170 for 86-88.<P>The 6869 and 7170 are the same circuitry, only the program code in the processor is different. It has a few minor refinements but nothing cosmic. But these difference are why you can't use a 6869 chip in a 7170 and vice-versa.||||reg||1
